{
  "_doc": [
    "Every SR arm the evaluators and orchestrators know: what method it is, how it is shown, what it is compared with, and where its config and checkpoints are.",
    "Read by variants/util/arms.py (Python) and Get-ArmInfo / Get-DisplayName in variants/util/lib.ps1 (PowerShell, ConvertFrom-Json).",
    "A tag may carry a step suffix (render_r1_40k): the entry of its base tag applies and the step is appended to the display name.",
    "methods.<m>: display = the method name in sheets; key_prefix = the column key prefix in reports (dt_ for DeepTextures: existing report keys);",
    "  checkpoint = tf | torch | none (how a step is found: tf = <prefix>.index files).",
    "arms.<tag>: method, display (row name), reference (the arm it is compared against; null = none),",
    "  config (repo-relative), checkpoint_root (container path; 'from_config' = the config's checkpoint_root key; {RSMOKE} = the smoke root of run.ps1).",
    "head_to_head: arm-vs-arm comparisons, in report order. A report shows the pairs whose two arms it was given (the map report: the first such pair).",
    "torch arms (variants/sr_finetune/): config null = zero-shot, nothing trained; checkpoint_root = where the weight files are (the official file, or the trainer's models/ folder);",
    "  their arm folders are written by sr_finetune/write_arm.py, never through Get-ArmInfo (which reads a DeepTextures yaml)."
  ],
